#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:2
msgid "Unix Makefiles"
msgstr "Unix Makefiles"

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:4
msgid "Generates standard UNIX makefiles."
msgstr "生成標準的 UNIX makefiles。"

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:6
msgid ""
"A hierarchy of UNIX makefiles is generated into the build tree.  Use any "
"standard UNIX-style make program to build the project through the ``all`` "
"target and install the project through the ``install`` (or ``install/"
"strip``) target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:11
msgid ""
"For each subdirectory ``sub/dir`` of the project a UNIX makefile will be "
"created, containing the following targets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:14
msgid "``all``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:15
msgid "Depends on all targets required by the subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:17
msgid "``install``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:18
msgid "Runs the install step in the subdirectory, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:20
msgid "``install/strip``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:21
msgid ""
"Runs the install step in the subdirectory followed by a ``CMAKE_STRIP`` "
"command, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:24
msgid ""
"The ``CMAKE_STRIP`` variable will contain the platform's ``strip`` utility, "
"which removes symbols information from generated binaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:27
msgid "``test``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:28
msgid "Runs the test step in the subdirectory, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:30
msgid "``package``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:31
msgid "Runs the package step in the subdirectory, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:33
msgid "``install_prep/<component>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:37
msgid ""
"Created if the project has install rules, unless the :variable:"
"`CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_PREP_TARGETS` or :variable:`CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RULES` "
"variable is enabled. Builds all known build dependencies for the named "
"install component. Components whose names cannot be represented safely are "
"excluded. See :ref:`Install Preparation Targets` and :ref:`Target Names`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:44
msgid "``install_prep/all``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:48
msgid ""
"Created if the project has install rules, unless the :variable:"
"`CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_PREP_TARGETS` or :variable:`CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RULES` "
"variable is enabled. Builds all known build dependencies for an installation "
"that does not select a component. See :ref:`Install Preparation Targets`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:54
msgid "``test_prep/<test-name>``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:58
msgid ""
"Created unless the :variable:`CMAKE_SKIP_TEST_PREP_TARGETS` variable is "
"enabled. Builds all known build dependencies for the named test, including "
"the executable target invoked by the test, targets referenced by generator "
"expressions in the test command, and explicit ``BUILD_DEPENDS`` entries. A "
"``BUILD_DEPENDS`` file is built by building the target whose build produces "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:65
msgid ""
"Tests with names that are not valid target names, and tests whose names "
"contain a ``:`` character, are excluded. If multiple tests in different "
"directories share the same name, their dependencies are merged into one "
"``test_prep/<test-name>`` target. See the :manual:`cmake-buildsystem(7)` "
"manual for more details on :ref:`Target Names`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:71
msgid ""
"Individual ``test_prep/<test-name>`` targets are not created for tests "
"discovered at test time, because their names are not known during generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:75
msgid "``test_prep/all``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../generator/Unix Makefiles.rst:79
msgid ""
"Created unless the :variable:`CMAKE_SKIP_TEST_PREP_TARGETS` variable is "
"enabled. Depends on every generated ``test_prep/<test-name>`` target. Also "
"builds dependencies recorded by the :prop_dir:`CMAKE_TEST_BUILD_DEPENDS` "
"directory property."
msgstr ""
